  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff in July 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and an additional $15,000 for training. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype and the completion of the testing phase. The project is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology and has updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January. A compliance plan budget of $55,000 has been approved. Upcoming events include a meeting on August 5th to discuss findings, a team meeting on August 1st for budget details, and a celebration on October 10th for the testing milestone."
